Part 4: Ammunition, Cooldowns, & Resource Logistics Matrix
1. Infinite vs. Finite Ammunition Architecture
Infinite Ammo Units: Light energy weapons and defensive point-defense systems (e.g., Viper Lasers, Assault Gunship Rotary Cannons, Ion Disablers, Command Escort Point-Defense) operate on standardized fire cycles with built-in heat cooldowns requiring zero resource restocking.

Finite Ammo Units: Heavy siege and specialized ordnance platforms (e.g., Lancer Railguns with 10 slugs, Heavy Torpedo Bombers, Vortex Minelayers with 50 mines, Relay Warp Frigates with 10 warp canisters) consume physical inventory per attack.

2. The Supply Tender Resupply Loop
Resource Synthesis: Supply Tenders (3W) hold automated manufacturing bays that convert raw materials (Metal, Ore, Isotopes, Plasma Gas, Graviton Cores) into specific finite ammunition types on-the-fly.

Field Delivery: When telemetry flags a combat unit's magazine or cache dropping below critical thresholds, a Supply Tender vectors directly to the unit, establishing a wireless fabrication tether to replenish ammunition without requiring a return trip to port.

